= Introduction <introduction>

There's long been a general understanding that there is discrepancy between transcriptomics and proteomics - only around 40% of variation in proteome data can be explained by its preceeding transcriptome counterpart although one originates from the other, and both traces back to their "blueprint" the DNA @vogel2012 @crick1970.

This discrepancy may pose a significant challenge for research regarding medicine aimed at treating glioblastoma (GBM) which historically already has poor survivability @lemee2018, as it creates an unclear target for GBM medicine research.

The research conducted aims to statistically compare and contrast transcriptomics and proteomics of GBM via differential analysis of their respective expression data against healthy brain tissue.
Chapter @background presents the relevant knowledge regarding the thesis's topic, including the biological entity of interest - glioblastoma, and multiomics.